// Test-suite type-check configuration.
//
// Extends the package tsconfig so the specs stay under the same `strict`
// family as the library, with the two index-signature guards relaxed. Both are
// load-bearing for src/ — the registry is a name-keyed lookup and the pipeline
// walks an array by index — and hostile to tests, which index into the default
// parser lists and assert on thrown messages, where a null-check at every site
// would bury the thing under test.
//
// The library keeps both guards (see ../tsconfig.json, which covers src/).
// Only the test tree opts out.
//
// There is no `../src/*.d.ts` to pull in any more. The one that corrected
// `@nodable/entities`' declaration of `EntityDecoder` as the module's *default*
// export is gone: the entity code is a workspace package that exports it by
// name and types it itself.
{
  "extends": "../tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": { "noPropertyAccessFromIndexSignature": false, "noUncheckedIndexedAccess": false },
  "include": ["./**/*.ts"]
}
